 ## Automatic retries
 
+**1.0 candidate:** mutating requests are sent once. A timeout, HTTP 429/5xx or
+unusable reply can mean the change was applied, so Tagcast never blindly sends that
+mutation again. This includes ordinary metadata and Cleanup, ratings, artwork
+assignments, playlist changes, tags, lyrics, trash, album merging and play reporting.
+
+Ordinary metadata saves stop later requests and check attempted values against a
+fresh library. A matching result can be confirmed; a mismatch or failed read-back
+stays unconfirmed. Other reviewed workflows retain their own partial/uncertain
+result handling. A lost response alone is neither success nor definite failure.
+Read-back establishes current values; it does not make remote saves transactional.
+
+Safe library/status/artwork/userdata reads can retain bounded retries after 2 and
+6 seconds. Explicit authentication rejection can refresh the sign-in separately.
+An image upload with a lost reply is not automatically repeated or assigned.
+
+**Do not immediately repeat an uncertain save manually.** Inspect the current
+library, then make a fresh review and conflict check before another change.
+
+<details>
+<summary>Earlier public releases (0.80.0–0.85.1)</summary>
+
+These downloads predate the candidate's send-once transport correction. The
+following historical behaviour is retained for users who have not upgraded:
+
 **A retry within a running request is different from repeating a finished save.** For selected operations, temporary network errors, HTTP 429 and 5xx responses trigger at most two further attempts, after **2 and 6 seconds**. Other operations send once because an ambiguous response could otherwise duplicate an action or overwrite a newer state.
 
 | Operation | Temporary-error retry behaviour in 0.80.0 |
@@ -41,6 +65,9 @@
 | Lyrics saves and lyrics-file import saves; tag operations; trash moves; play reporting | No automatic temporary-error retry. |
 
 After an operation finishes with an uncertain result, Tagcast does not schedule it to run again by itself. **Do not immediately repeat it manually.** Read the result and inspect the current library first. A new review is required for any further change. These transport rules are separate from refreshing an expired sign-in.
