+## Desktop Mini Player
+
+**Unreleased; included in the local 1.0 candidate.** Choose **View → Open Mini
+Player**, press **Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+M**, or choose **Mini Player** in expanded Now
+playing. Artwork and track information sit above transport and a track-relative
+seek bar. Pin keeps the window on top where supported; it is unavailable on
+Linux/Wayland. Window bounds and Pin are remembered in the desktop profile.
+
+Opening it hides the main window. **Open Tagcast**, closing the Mini Player or
+returning to the main window restores the full interface and closes the compact
+window. Playback continues through the same audio element and queue, including
+supported experimental Gapless playback. It does not create a second player.
+Normal Quit still stops the app; existing unsaved-change warnings apply.
+Python/browser use retains its existing player.
